{
  "id": "minimax-h3-10eros-pack",
  "name": "Community — MiniMax H3 (10Eros Max)",
  "version": "2.0.1",
  "author": "DmitryDB",
  "nsfw": true,
  "description": "MiniMax H3 on the 10Eros Max finetune, INT8 ConvRot build for RTX 30/40. Non-pruned weights: faster than the stock base despite being larger, because fewer layers need per-step dequantisation. Text-to-video, image-to-video and reference-to-video, all on one model file. The Turbo variants moved to their own pack, MiniMax H3 (10Eros Max, Turbo).",
  "tags": [
    "Local",
    "Video",
    "T2V",
    "MiniMax H3",
    "Finetune",
    "10Eros"
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "id": "minimax-h3-10eros-t2v",
      "name": "MiniMax H3 Text to Video (10Eros Max)",
      "icon": "🎬",
      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "The 10Eros Max finetune of MiniMax H3 (INT8 ConvRot build), run through the unmodified official T2V graph — same sampler, scheduler and step count as the stock preset, so the model is the only difference.\n\nThis is the non-pruned base: full-width adaln (96768x16 against the stock 96768x8) and 30 layers left in BF16 that the stock weights store as int8.\n\nMeasured on SimpliGen 1.50.0 / engine v0.33.1, 5s/480p/20 steps on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti with ~19 GB system RAM free: 113.3s against the official preset's 113.2s on the beta engine (e5a38e3, 2026-08-27, warm, seed-fixed, n=1) - a dead heat. The 4% edge measured on engine v0.33.1 (119.1s vs 123.5s) no longer holds. Note it is actually SLOWER per sampling step (3.60s vs 3.01s) and wins only on load overhead.\n\nOn builds before 1.50.0 the gap was far larger (133.4s vs 171.4s, 22%). That was a VRAM-pressure artifact: while the run was memory-bound, streaming dominated and hid the per-step cost. 1.50.0 frees the text encoder before sampling, and most of the advantage went with it. If you are on an older build, expect the bigger number.\n\nWeights are 20.94 GiB. Free system RAM matters more than VRAM here — keep 16 GB+ free or timings degrade sharply.",
